# Preserve these bytes exactly as CocoaPods emitted them.
#
# This directory is a SNAPSHOT of tool output held as licence evidence, so its
# value is that it is what the tool produced. Git's default text handling would
# normalise the CRLF line endings in the acknowledgement files on commit and
# re-expand them on checkout, which means the tracked copy no longer hashes to
# the file that was captured and a digest comparison against the source becomes
# meaningless.
#
# This is not hypothetical here: on 2026-08-14 the published FFmpeg
# corresponding-source archives had to be regenerated and republished because
# `git archive` had silently applied EOL conversion to them - 15 CR-terminated
# shebangs in libzvbi alone. Same class of defect, same day, different tool.
#
# Evidence is bytes. Do not remove this file.
* -text
